CFG_BONDING_MODE|CFG_BONDING_MODE|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Define Bonding modes Possible values: - No-bonding mode(0x00) - Bonding mode(0x01)
CFG_FIXED_PIN|CFG_FIXED_PIN|Application configuration - Application parameters||0|999999|Any random value between 0 and 999999
CFG_USED_FIXED_PIN|CFG_USED_FIXED_PIN|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Define Fixed Pin option, if set to 1 then CFG_FIXED_PIN will be ignored
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|Application configuration - Application parameters||=CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|16|Encryption key maximum size
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|Application configuration - Application parameters||7|16|Encryption key minimum size
CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Define IO capabilities
CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Activate/deactivate Define Man In The Middle(MITM) protection mode Possible values: - MITM protection not required (0x00) - MITM protection required (0x01)
CFG_SC_SUPPORT|CFG_SC_SUPPORT|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Define Secure Connections Support Possible values: - Secure Connections Paring not supported (0x00) - Secure Connections Paring supported but optional (0x01) - Secure Connections Paring supported and mandatory(0x02)
CFG_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION_SUPPORT|GAP_KEYPRESS_NOT_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Define Keypress notification support
CFG_GAP_APPEARANCE|CFG_GAP_APPEARANCE|Application configuration - Application parameters||||
CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME|CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME|Application configuration - Application parameters||||Device name; default value is TEMPLATE
CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME_LENGTH|CFG_GAP_DEVICE_NAME_LENGTH|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|48|Device name lenght; max value is 48bytes, default value is 8 (TEMPLATE length)
CFG_SCAN_INT_MS|CFG_SCAN_INT_MS|Application configuration - Application parameters||2.500|40959.375|Duration in ms of the scan on the primary advertising channel
CFG_SCAN_WIN_MS|CFG_SCAN_WIN_MS|Application configuration - Application parameters||2.500|40959.375|Time interval in ms from when the Controller started its last scan until it begins the subsequent scan on the primary advertising physical channel
BLE_CFG_MAX_NBR_GATT_EVT_HANDLERS|BLE_CFG_MAX_NBR_GATT_EVT_HANDLERS|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|255|Maximum number of GATT event handlers that can be registered
CFG_BLE_NUM_CLIENT_CONTEXTS|CFG_BLE_NUM_CLIENT_CONTEXTS|Application configuration - Application parameters||1|64|Maximum number of Client contexts. It must be set to the maximum number of simultaneous connected servers.
CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|Application configuration - BLE stack||0||Maximum number of attributes that can be stored in the GATT database in addition to the attributes number already defined for the GATT and GAP services (BLE_STACK_NUM_GATT_MANDATORY_ATTRIBUTES value on STM32_BLE middleware, ble_stack.h header file). One attribute is required for each: service declaration characteristic declaration characteristic value characteristic descriptor NOTES: - if a characteristic has the notify or indicate property set, then a client characteristic configuration descriptor is required. - if a characteristic has the broadcast property set, then a server characteristic configuration descriptor is required. - if a characteristic has the extended property set, then a characteristic extended property descriptor is required.
CFG_BLE_NUM_RADIO_TASKS|CFG_BLE_NUM_RADIO_TASKS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Maximum number of simultaneous connections that the device will support
GATT_CLT_MAX_NUM_SERVERS|GATT_CLT_MAX_NUM_SERVERS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||
CFG_BLE_NUM_OF_CONCURRENT_GATT_CLIENT_PROC|CFG_BLE_NUM_OF_CONCURRENT_GATT_CLIENT_PROC|Application configuration - BLE stack|||=CFG_BLE_NUM_RADIO_TASKS|Maximum number of concurrent Client's Procedures. This value must be less than or equal to the maximum number of supported links (CFG_BLE_NUM_RADIO_TASKS)
CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|255|Maximum number of channels in LE credit based flow control mode
CFG_BLE_NUM_EATT_CHANNELS|CFG_BLE_NUM_EATT_CHANNELS|Application configuration - BLE stack|||=CFG_BLE_COC_NBR_MAX|Maximum number of simultaneously EATT channels the stack should support
CFG_BLE_ATT_MTU_MAX|CFG_BLE_ATT_MTU_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||23|1020|Maximum supported ATT_MTU size
CFG_BLE_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH_MAX|CFG_BLE_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack|||4294967295|Maximum duration of the connection event when the device is in slave mode in units of 625/256 us (~2.44 us)
CFG_BLE_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH_MAX_HEXA|CFG_BLE_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH_MAX_HEXA|Application configuration - BLE stack|||0xFFFFFFFF|Maximum duration of the connection event when the device is in slave mode in units of 625/256 us (~2.44 us)
RFWKPCLKSOURCE|RFWKPCLKSOURCE|Application configuration - BLE stack||||
CFG_BLE_SLEEP_CLOCK_ACCURACY|CFG_BLE_SLEEP_CLOCK_ACCURACY|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Sleep clock accuracy
CFG_BLE_MBLOCK_COUNT_MARGIN|CFG_BLE_MBLOCK_COUNT_MARGIN|Application configuration - BLE stack||0||Number of extra memory blocks, in addition to the minimum required for the supported links
CFG_BLE_NUM_ADV_SETS|CFG_BLE_NUM_ADV_SETS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Maximum number of advertising data set
CFG_BLE_NUM_AUX_SCAN_SLOTS|CFG_BLE_NUM_AUX_SCAN_SLOTS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Maximum number of slots for scanning on the secondary advertising channel
CFG_BLE_NUM_PAWR_SUBEVENTS|CFG_BLE_NUM_PAWR_SUBEVENTS|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|128|Maximum number of Periodic Advertising with Responses subevents.
CFG_BLE_PAWR_SUBEVENT_DATA_COUNT_MAX|CFG_BLE_PAWR_SUBEVENT_DATA_COUNT_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|=MIN(15, CFG_BLE_NUM_PAWR_SUBEVENTS)|Maximum number of subevent data that can be queued in the controller.
CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_SLOTS|CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_SLOTS|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Maximum number of slots to be synchronized
CFG_BLE_FILTER_ACCEPT_LIST_SIZE_LOG2|CFG_BLE_FILTER_ACCEPT_LIST_SIZE_LOG2|Application configuration - BLE stack||||Two's logarithm of the white/resolving list size
CFG_BLE_COC_MPS_MAX|CFG_BLE_COC_MPS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|1024|The maximum size of payload data in octets that the L2CAP layer entity can accept
CFG_BLE_NUM_CTE_ANTENNA_IDS_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_CTE_ANTENNA_IDS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|0|Maximum number of antenna IDs in the antenna pattern
CFG_BLE_NUM_CTE_IQ_SAMPLES_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_CTE_IQ_SAMPLES_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|0|Maximum number of IQ samples in the buffer used in CTE connection oriented mode.
CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_BIG_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_BIG_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|1|Maximum number of slots for synchronizing to a Broadcast Isochronous Group.
CFG_BLE_NUM_BRC_BIG_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_BRC_BIG_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|1|Maximum number of slots for broadcasting a Broadcast Isochronous Group.
CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_BIS_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_SYNC_BIS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|2|Maximum number of slots for synchronizing to a Broadcast Isochronous Stream.
CFG_BLE_NUM_BRC_BIS_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_BRC_BIS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|2|Maximum number of slots for broadcasting a Broadcast Isochronous Stream.
CFG_BLE_NUM_CIG_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_CIG_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|2|Maximum number of Connected Isochronous Groups
CFG_BLE_NUM_CIS_MAX|CFG_BLE_NUM_CIS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||1|2|Description: Maximum number of Connected Isochronous Streams
CFG_BLE_ISR0_FIFO_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ISR0_FIFO_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||1||Size of the internal FIFO used for critical controller events produced by the ISR
CFG_BLE_ISR1_FIFO_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ISR0_FIFO_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||1||Size of the internal FIFO used for noncritical controller events produced by the ISR
CFG_BLE_USER_FIFO_SIZE|CFG_BLE_USER_FIFO_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||1||Size of the internal FIFO used for controller and host events produced outside the ISR
CFG_BLE_GAP_PERIPH_PREF_CONN_PARAM_CHARACTERISTIC|CFG_BLE_GAP_PERIPH_PREF_CONN_PARAM_CHARACTERISTIC|Application configuration - BLE stack||||If 1, Peripheral Preferred Connection Parameters Characteristic is added in GAP service.
CFG_BLE_GAP_ENCRYPTED_KEY_MATERIAL_CHARACTERISTIC|CFG_BLE_GAP_ENCRYPTED_KEY_MATERIAL_CHARACTERISTIC|Application configuration - BLE stack||||If 1, Encrypted Key Material Characteristic is added in GAP service.
CFG_BLE_EXTRA_LL_PROCEDURE_CONTEXTS|CFG_BLE_EXTRA_LL_PROCEDURE_CONTEXTS|Application configuration - BLE stack||0|128|Maximum number of simultaneous Link Layer procedures that can be managed, in addition to the minimum required by the stack. The minimum number guarantees one LL procedure initiated by the peer for each link, one LL procedure automatically initiated by the Controller and one LL procedure initiated by the Host.
CFG_BLE_ATT_QUEUED_WRITE_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ATT_QUEUED_WRITE_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||0||Size of buffer used for ATT queued writes
CFG_BLE_GATT_NWK_BUFFER_SIZE|CFG_BLE_GATT_NWK_BUFFER_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||200||Amount of RAM used to store GATT services (bytes)
CFG_BLE_ADV_NWK_BUFFER_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ADV_NWK_BUFFER_SIZE|Application configuration - BLE stack||40||Amount of RAM used to store advertising data (bytes)
CFG_BLE_GATT_CLT_NUM_CHARAC_SUBSCRIPTIONS_MAX|CFG_BLE_GATT_CLT_NUM_CHARAC_SUBSCRIPTIONS_MAX|Application configuration - BLE stack||0||Maximum number of characteristics that can be subscribed to check for security level
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_SCAN_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_SCAN_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE master capabilities support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CTE_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CTE_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Constant tone extension support on device providing the related HW capability (AoA, Aod direction finding features)
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PRIVACY_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PRIVACY_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Controller Privacy support.
CFG_BLE_SECURE_CONNECTIONS_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_SECURE_CONNECTIONS_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE secure connections support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_DATA_LENGTH_EXTENSION_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_DATA_LENGTH_EXTENSION_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE data length extension support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_2M_CODED_PHY_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_2M_CODED_PHY_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE 2M and LE Coded PHYs support.
CFG_BLE_L2CAP_COS_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_L2CAP_COS_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE L2CAP-COS support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_EXT_ADV_SCAN_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_EXT_ADV_SCAN_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the extended advertsing and scanning support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PERIODIC_ADV_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PERIODIC_ADV_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Periodic Advertising and Synchronizer support
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PERIODIC_ADV_WR_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_PERIODIC_ADV_WR_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Periodic Advertising with Responses
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_POWER_CONTROL_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_POWER_CONTROL_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Power Control and PATH Loss Monitoring support.
CFG_BLE_CONNECTION_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONNECTION_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE Power Control and PATH Loss Monitoring support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CHAN_CLASS_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CHAN_CLASS_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE channel calssification support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_BIS_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_BIS_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE broadcast isochronous support.
CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CIS_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONTROLLER_CIS_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE connection isochronous support.
CFG_BLE_CONNECTION_SUBRATING_ENABLED|CFG_BLE_CONNECTION_SUBRATING_ENABLED|Application configuration - Modular Options||||Enable/disable the Bluetooth LE conection subrating support.
CFG_FULL_LOW_POWER|CFG_FULL_LOW_POWER|Application configuration - Low Power||||
CFG_LPM_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_SUPPORTED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Low Power mode: When set to 1, the low power mode is Enabled When set to 0, the device stays in RUN mode
CFG_LPM_EMULATED|CFG_LPM_EMULATED|Application configuration - Low Power||||Low Power mode emulated (DeepStop2): When set to 1, the low power mode emulated is Enabled, provided that CFG_LPM_SUPPORTED is set to 1. When set to 0, the low power mode emulated is not Enabled.
CFG_DEBUG_APP_TRACE|CFG_DEBUG_APP_TRACE|Application configuration - Traces||||Enable or disable traces in application
CFG_DEBUG_APP_ADV_TRACE|CFG_DEBUG_APP_ADV_TRACE|Application configuration - Traces||||Enable or disable traces in application
ADV_TRACE_TIMESTAMP_ENABLE|ADV_TRACE_TIMESTAMP_ENABLE|Application configuration - Traces||||Enable or disable traces in application
RT_DEBUG_GPIO_MODULE|RT_DEBUG_GPIO_MODULE|Application configuration - Debug||||Real Time Debug GPIO module configuration
BLE_TRANSPARENT_MODE_UART|BLE_TRANSPARENT_MODE_UART|Application configuration - Traces||||Enable or disable communication with STM32Cube Monitor RF
